1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,664
A new bank signs the contract on a Monday.

2
00:00:02,714 --> 00:00:08,688
Its platform team gets two empty Linux hosts: one in the test zone, and one in the production zone.

3
00:00:08,738 --> 00:00:12,768
What has to happen before Aziz can type his phone number for the first time?

4
00:00:12,818 --> 00:00:18,528
Lesson 4 gave the configuration, and Lesson 21 closed the trail with the audit.

5
00:00:18,578 --> 00:00:24,000
Now the whole platform goes into that bank, and Aziz walks his journey one last time.

6
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:28,632
Each zone gets one Linux host, and each host runs its own installation.

7
00:00:28,682 --> 00:00:34,176
Each unit is an image, and Docker Compose runs one copy of each image on the host.

8
00:00:34,226 --> 00:00:36,792
This set of units is the Compose stack.

9
00:00:36,842 --> 00:00:45,696
In front run the two gateways, Keycloak, the workers, and four adapters: MyID, TAF, SMS and push.

10
00:00:45,746 --> 00:00:51,672
Behind them run Postgres, Valkey, Kafka and Vault, and each one is new for that zone.

11
00:00:51,722 --> 00:00:54,744
Then OpenTofu does what Lesson 4 showed.

12
00:00:54,794 --> 00:01:00,624
It gives the deploy values of the zone, and the defaults for every policy and every text.

13
00:01:00,674 --> 00:01:04,800
It also writes the settings and the secrets of each unit into Vault.

14
00:01:04,850 --> 00:01:08,184
An install script reads them from Vault and starts the stack.

15
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:12,048
If one value is missing, the start stops with a clear error.

16
00:01:12,098 --> 00:01:15,912
Vault starts sealed: it holds the keys, but it cannot use them.

17
00:01:15,962 --> 00:01:20,976
It opens only with the unseal keys, and the bank's security team keeps them.

18
00:01:21,026 --> 00:01:25,632
So the platform team starts the stack, and the security team opens Vault.

19
00:01:25,682 --> 00:01:28,968
Now the stack runs, but customers still cannot come in.

20
00:01:29,018 --> 00:01:34,824
The installation opens for customers only when the bank has at least one active app with a required level.

21
00:01:34,874 --> 00:01:36,960
Here that app is the mobile bank.

22
00:01:37,010 --> 00:01:40,584
Until then, the platform refuses every journey.

23
00:01:40,634 --> 00:01:48,216
The admin panel also lists each policy and text that still has its default value, so the bank sees what it has not decided yet.

24
00:01:48,266 --> 00:01:50,832
Stage, in the test zone, goes first.

25
00:01:50,882 --> 00:01:54,624
And here is one more fact about Aziz: he is not a real person.

26
00:01:54,674 --> 00:01:59,232
The test team needs him every day, so in stage he is a test identity.

27
00:01:59,282 --> 00:02:09,312
A test identity is a record in the MyID test environment, with a known result: success, or a named failure, such as a face that does not match.

28
00:02:09,362 --> 00:02:14,280
Each night, the acceptance tests run in stage against these test identities.

29
00:02:14,330 --> 00:02:20,928
Stage connects only to the MyID test environment, and each customer that it creates carries a test mark.

30
00:02:20,978 --> 00:02:24,216
Limits and reports never count test customers.

31
00:02:24,266 --> 00:02:32,592
Production connects only to the real MyID, and there every customer is a real person, even the people that the bank uses for its own checks.

32
00:02:32,642 --> 00:02:35,880
No network route joins the two zones.

33
00:02:35,930 --> 00:02:42,048
Only configuration moves from stage to production, as a difference that a second person approves.

34
00:02:42,098 --> 00:02:46,272
Customers, devices, sessions and audit events never move.

35
00:02:46,322 --> 00:02:52,992
And production guards itself: it does not start with a test address for MyID, or when test customers are allowed.

36
00:02:53,042 --> 00:02:56,376
Its database refuses any customer with the test mark.

37
00:02:56,426 --> 00:02:58,944
Developers do not wait for a zone.

38
00:02:58,994 --> 00:03:02,016
The same stack runs on a laptop with one command.

39
00:03:02,066 --> 00:03:11,424
The simulators of Lesson 5 play MyID, TAF, the SMS vendor and the push service, so the tests run with no internet.

40
00:03:11,474 --> 00:03:15,528
On the laptop, Aziz is a simulator that never gets tired.

41
00:03:15,578 --> 00:03:20,088
The installation is done only when each line of a short list can be checked.

42
00:03:20,138 --> 00:03:22,416
The decisions are written and accepted.

43
00:03:22,466 --> 00:03:25,344
The contracts of both gateways are published.

44
00:03:25,394 --> 00:03:27,360
Each failure path has a test.

45
00:03:27,410 --> 00:03:32,184
Audit events reach the stream, and a stand-in for the bank's monitoring reads them.

46
00:03:32,234 --> 00:03:37,632
The code has a review, and the release has an independent security review and a penetration test.

47
00:03:37,682 --> 00:03:41,832
The guides for the app teams and for the people who run the platform exist.

48
00:03:41,882 --> 00:03:48,576
The full acceptance run passes in stage, against the simulators and the MyID test identities.

49
00:03:48,626 --> 00:03:53,592
And the product manager signs off after a demo on real phones in the test zone.

50
00:03:53,642 --> 00:03:57,936
Now suppose that a test identity tries to reach the production zone.

51
00:03:57,986 --> 00:03:59,808
What happens?

52
00:03:59,858 --> 00:04:07,320
Nothing gets in: production talks only to the real MyID, and its database refuses any customer with the test mark.

53
00:04:07,370 --> 00:04:09,912
Now walk Aziz's journey one last time.

54
00:04:09,962 --> 00:04:16,728
On a Sunday he registered with his number, a code through TAF and a password, and reached level one.

55
00:04:16,778 --> 00:04:20,040
On a Saturday he wanted to send money to his mother.

56
00:04:20,090 --> 00:04:27,072
He gave his consent and passed MyID, and TAF confirmed that his number was his own: level two.

57
00:04:27,122 --> 00:04:29,304
His phone became his one money phone.

58
00:04:29,354 --> 00:04:35,016
He logged out because of his nephew, and logged in again on the same phone, with his password and a code.

59
00:04:35,066 --> 00:04:40,416
When he lost the phone, one operator blocked it, and a second operator approved the unblock.

60
00:04:40,466 --> 00:04:43,248
Months later, the audit answered his letter.

61
00:04:43,298 --> 00:04:49,272
Each of those steps runs inside one bank, in one installation, on one host in each zone.

62
00:04:49,322 --> 00:04:52,248
Prove once, then bind: that is heeyID.

63
00:04:52,298 --> 00:04:57,672
The next module adds the one step that Aziz still cannot take alone: a new phone.
